WEBVTT

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.280
Yuzu-chan, hurry up!

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:38.730
<b>Sweet Bitter Potato</b>

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:38.740
Momo, you don't have to run so fast.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.050
Yes, I do.

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:44.730
The school store's sweet 
potatoes are really popular.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:47.840
They sold out yesterday, 
and I couldn't get any.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.210
Your dedication to food is amazing.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.460
<b>School Store</b>

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:55.310
I'll take three sweet potatoes.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:58.510
This whole line is for sweet potatoes?

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:00.410
It's like a fancy delicatessen in a mall.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:05.140
Sweet Potatoes

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.970
We're almost there!

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:09.310
You'll finally get your potatoes.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:12.150
Maximum of 3 Sweet 
Potatoes per person

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.150
Two sweet potatoes—

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:13.650
Sweet potatoes are now sold out.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:13.650
<b>Out of sweet potatoes</b>

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:15.190
What?!

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:18.270
Aww, they're out...

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:20.040
We waited so long, too...

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:20.880
We're sorry.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:21.780
Momoko.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:22.700
Huh?

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:24.940
Nagiko-chan-senpai.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:26.950
Oh, good. I've been looking for you.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.840
Do you have some time?

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.960
You kind of look like you've 
given up on the world.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:34.560
I'm okay, really.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.540
Yuzu-chan and I came to 
buy some sweet potatoes,

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:41.210
but they ran out as soon as we got there,
so I'm just disappointed.

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:42.440
Nice to meet you.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:44.970
I'm an old friend of Momo's, Yuzuko Hazuki.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.390
Thanks for looking after Momo.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:50.100
Please, no need to exaggerate.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:53.330
I'm a second-year in the 
light music club, Kurokawa.

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:54.480
Nice to meet you.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:58.740
So, what did you need, Nagiko-chan-senpai?

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:03.520
Oh, right... Did you turn in 
the light music club activity log?

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:05.870
Actually, I haven't yet...

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:07.650
I thought as much.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:10.870
The teacher's looking for it, 
so please submit it soon.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:13.750
I'm sorry about that...

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:16.640
You don't have to get so upset.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:19.210
I couldn't buy my sweet potatoes,

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:21.880
and I forgot to submit the activity log...

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.130
Bad things just keep happening...

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:27.140
No, as far as the log goes, 
you just forgot to turn it in.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.850
Anyway, don't forget.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.350
Okay. I'm sorry.

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:36.410
President Mishima!

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:38.360
Oh... Uh...

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:41.650
I'm Akari Amari, a first-year from the occult club.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:44.040
I might be the president and not at club much,

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:46.080
but I still know who you are.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:49.850
What brings you to the third-years' building?

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:51.210
Look at this!

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:56.290
<b>The 1984 Log of All Club Activity</b>

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:56.290
The 1984 Log of All Club Activity?

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.700
That's pretty old.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:05.000
There's a strange code written in the 
occult research club's log for this year.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.430
Let's see...

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:10.020
"Forge lost connections,

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:13.310
and lead the people to the cafeteria."

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:16.060
What is this supposed to mean?

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.890
Well, if I remember correctly...

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:23.920
I think I've heard of a code that 
described how to solve a problem

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.700
that came up in the occult club a long time ago.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.020
Maybe that's it.

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:29.370
A problem?

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.400
Like all of the club's members

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.290
turned into zombies, except the president?!

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.580
That'd be an awfully grim situation...

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:40.410
I don't really know the details, though.

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:43.260
I'm like a ghost president, you know.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:46.280
If you're looking into it, good luck.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:47.840
I see...

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:50.430
Thank you.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:53.180
<b>Faculty Room</b>

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.180
Sorry to interrupt.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:59.320
Hmm... I guess I'll go tell Nagiko-chan-senpai 
that I submitted the log.

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:01.830
You're really something, Kurokawa-san.

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:03.190
How so?

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:07.140
You were talking to that girl 
in the school store earlier.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:09.880
Oh, you mean the first-year 
from the light music club?

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:11.120
Who?

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.200
Her name's Momoko.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:15.480
It was like you were talking with a friend.

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:19.780
I don't really pay attention to 
who's older and who's younger.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:23.650
If anything, people might think 
that makes you unreliable.

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.720
Yeah, if we're talking about you, Haruka.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:29.010
H-Huh? Am I unreliable?

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:33.810
I can't talk to older students 
like you do. I get scared.

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:38.360
Well, this year's first-years are really 
energetic, or just do as they please.

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:41.820
Some of them are pretty airheaded, too.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:43.440
So it can be a pain to deal with.

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:45.360
<i>A pain?</i>

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.880
And it's terribly rude for people to
assume we're unreliable, too.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:51.280
<i>Rude...</i>

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.330
What are you doing?

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.620
Class is about to start.

00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:57.760
R-Right...

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:05.800
What's wrong?

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:10.030
Are you that depressed because you 
didn't get any sweet potatoes?

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.440
Am I a pain?

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.100
Am I rude?

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:15.640
Huh?

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:18.830
Am I a pain for talking to older girls like friends,

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:23.080
and being energetic and airheaded 
and doing as I please?

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:24.610
Huh?

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:29.280
I wonder if I'm rude for not 
relying on the older girls, too...

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:32.370
Huh? What's wrong? What happened?

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:36.640
I see...

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:39.420
Kurokawa-senpai said all that?

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:42.670
I've been in the light music 
club for almost half a year.

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:45.990
I always thought we were getting along great.

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:50.590
Is it that bad to talk to her like we're friends?

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:56.600
I don't know if it's bad, but I guess 
treating a senpai as any other friend

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:00.030
kind of goes against etiquette.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:02.920
An athletic club would never let that happen.

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:03.940
I guess it's kinda rude.

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:08.020
So I <i>was</i> being rude...

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:09.510
Calm down.

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:13.320
I was just talking about how 
the athletic clubs operate.

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:13.820
Okay?

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:16.830
At this rate...

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:21.040
Her lousy manners make her annoying enough,

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.840
but she's an airhead, too. What a pain.

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:24.750
That's 50 push-ups for you!

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:26.880
No! I can't!

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:30.560
It might trim my upper arms, 
but I'd get all muscular!

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:33.760
What did you imagine that 
made you bring up muscles?

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:37.180
Maybe I need to stop coming across as airheaded?

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:41.060
I think you just need to speak a little more politely.

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:44.450
Um... To stop being airheaded...

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:47.710
Would the opposite of 
"airheaded" be "waterheaded"?

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:50.690
<b>(Aquaculture)</b>

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:50.690
Do I just need to be waterheaded?

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:53.450
She's doomed.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:03.460
Miyauchi-san.

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:09.760
Don't do that...

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:11.730
You scared me.

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:13.120
I'm sorry.

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:16.050
I wasn't going to attack you or anything.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:19.070
I <i>was</i> trying to scare you, though.

00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:22.430
It's bad enough that you meant to scare me.

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:25.340
So, did you need something?

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.320
Well, I was looking at this.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:31.120
What's this?

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:32.800
It looks like some sort of code.

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:33.450
Code?

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:35.670
Do you know what it means?

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:37.200
What it means...

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:41.060
No clue.

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:44.050
Don't just give up so easily.

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:46.790
Why are you asking me, anyway?

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:51.050
Well, Miyauchi-san, you're in the film research club.

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:53.280
If you're familiar with the suspense genre,

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:55.970
I thought you might know about this stuff.

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:59.720
I only watch movies that have
blood spraying everywhere!

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:02.890
That's quite a bias...

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:08.270
But I'm not too familiar with 
suspense, either, so I don't know.

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:10.410
I see...

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:12.650
Sorry to bother you.

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:16.030
Anyway, I just don't think I should bother anyone.

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:20.720
For Nagiko-chan-senpai and Haruka-chan-senpai,

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:22.510
and for the light music club...

00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:24.470
I need to change.

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:27.660
Well, you might be right,

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:31.040
but I don't think you can change just like that.

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:34.180
Then, what should I do?

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:39.050
I think it's important to show the older girls 
how much you appreciate them every day.

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:41.770
If you can do that,

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:44.350
you'll be showing them respect 
naturally, without being weird.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:46.560
I see...

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.370
If you can show them respect,

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:52.320
I'm sure you can restore a relationship 
of half a year, even if it was lost.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.530
That's it!

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:54.980
That's exactly it!

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:56.950
Forge lost connections!

00:09:57.550 --> 00:10:00.820
I'm sure the relationships between 
members of the occult research club

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:03.200
became rocky, and they were trying to fix them!

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:07.830
Right.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:12.160
"Forge lost connections,

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:15.520
and lead the people to the cafeteria."

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:19.590
This is talking about students 
forming stronger relationships?

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:20.640
That's right!

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:24.720
Mishima-senpai, the occult 
research club's "ghost president"...

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:30.580
I think I've heard of a code that 
described how to solve a problem

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:33.270
that came up in the occult club a long time ago.

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:35.040
...told me that.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:39.280
So I'm sure it's talking about getting 
students who were fighting to make up!

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:43.080
What about the "lead the people
 to the cafeteria" part, then?

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:48.410
I'm sure they all ate together 
there after they made up!

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:50.280
I understand where you're coming from,

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:51.930
but it sounds a bit contrived.

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:52.670
Right, Momo?

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:56.000
Lead the people to the cafeteria...

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:57.040
Huh?

00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:59.060
If we can solve that code,

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:02.800
I can make up with Nagiko-chan-senpai 
and Haruka-chan-senpai.

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:04.970
Is that what it means?

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:06.200
No, that's—

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:07.430
That's right!

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:11.260
I'm sure there's some sort of 
forbidden law in here that will let you

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:12.900
fix your relationships with the older girls!

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:16.110
We need to figure out the method!

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.450
No, that can't be...

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:20.840
There's almost no evidence.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:21.660
Right, Momo?

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:26.810
Let's solve this, Amari-san!

00:11:26.810 --> 00:11:28.870
Of course, Asahina-san!

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:33.460
It's no use. They're not even making sense now.

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:37.940
Hey, Miyauchi-san, say something...

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:42.720
I'm not really into mystery and suspense movies,

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:46.100
but this seems like a lot of fun!

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:46.960
Huh?!

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:49.180
I'll help out, too!

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:51.230
How did this happen?

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:54.190
Can you guys calm down just a little?

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:55.360
Excuse us!

00:11:56.520 --> 00:12:02.120
Um... Would you mind if we joined you?

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:05.280
Is it true that we can get 
along with the older girls?

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:09.110
Some things have happened in our club, too...

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:11.480
Sure. We'd love to welcome you.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:13.540
Let's all work together to solve the code,

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:16.170
and make up with the older girls!

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:18.040
Yeah!

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:26.170
Girl Friend BETA.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:33.440
Our first clue here is the keyword "cafeteria."

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:38.080
Yeah, it is the only word here 
that's pretty well-defined.

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:40.250
So, what should we do first?

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:46.440
I think we should start by introducing ourselves.

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:46.950
Huh?

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:50.410
Well, we're all in different classes and clubs.

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:52.580
We don't know what to call each other.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.610
We should do all of that right.

00:12:54.610 --> 00:12:58.500
If we have the time for that, 
we should use it to search for clues...

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:02.710
I'm Ichigo Kohinata from 
Class 1-B and the art club.

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:09.720
I feel happiest when I'm able 
to peel a peach perfectly.

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:14.290
I'm also from 1-B, Nae Yuuki, 
in the arts and crafts club.

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:16.350
I make cute mascot toys.

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:21.500
I'm Akari Amari of Class 1-C, 
in the occult research club.

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:24.360
I like zombies and blood splatters!

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:28.110
They really are introducing themselves...

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:32.490
Anyway, we just need to find out 
what happened in the cafeteria.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:35.290
We can check the school logs 
and graduation pictures...

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:38.330
Looking in the old school records 
is the only thing we can really do.

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:42.300
We don't have much to go on, do we?

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:44.400
Hey, look at that.

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:46.580
Graduation Albums

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:46.590
I think they're the graduation albums.

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:48.290
Yeah, they are.

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:50.110
Let's take a look.

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:56.120
Nae-chan, how tall are you, again?

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:00.330
143 centimeters...

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:02.620
Oh, I'm taller!

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:04.830
You're not that much taller, Momo.

00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:06.560
I'm taller by two centimeters.

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:08.220
It's not a contest.

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:11.140
Anyway, the tallest one here should get them.

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:12.820
Stare...

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:15.290
Me?

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:16.750
Okay, hold on.

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:20.920
There we go.

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:24.750
Ow...

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:26.720
What happened?

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:28.560
Sorry.

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:31.530
I was trying to pull a book off the top shelf,

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:33.470
and the other books fell, too.

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:37.600
Oh, in that case, you should
 have used a stepladder.

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:39.600
Yeah...

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:42.410
Are you looking for any book in particular?

00:14:42.410 --> 00:14:45.980
We're looking for any materials 
on the school cafeteria!

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:48.430
The cafeteria?

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:52.040
I've never seen anything like that.

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:54.040
Do you need it for something?

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:55.260
Yeah, this.

00:14:55.940 --> 00:15:00.730
Apparently, the occult research club ate 
together in the cafeteria a long time ago.

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:02.510
We wanted to know more about it.

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:05.710
But if there are no books on it, I guess we can't...

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:09.470
We don't have anything on the cafeteria,

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:12.970
but it looks like the page before this one is missing.

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:14.120
Huh?

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:16.760
You can read this part with a page missing,

00:15:16.760 --> 00:15:18.720
but since it looks like a code,

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:21.420
I'm sure something came before it.

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:22.350
What?!

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:23.520
Then...

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:25.510
If we know what was on the previous page,

00:15:25.510 --> 00:15:27.720
we might be able to figure this out!

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:29.860
Do you have the log for this club?

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:31.960
We don't have it here,

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:34.440
but I believe there's a copy upstairs in storage.

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:35.660
Yay!

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:38.200
Thank you very much!

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:51.920
Huh? The lights won't come on.

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:53.840
It's kinda creepy in here.

00:15:54.400 --> 00:15:56.930
It almost feels like a ghost could pop out.

00:15:58.740 --> 00:16:03.240
If this were a zombie movie, zombies would 
totally be waiting to ambush us here!

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:05.770
Don't say stuff like that...

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:12.080
Hm... It's not here.

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:15.000
Did you find it?

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:18.370
No, I thought they were peaches...

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:21.360
I don't think any would be up here.

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:23.400
Sorry.

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:24.410
Jeez.

00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:27.730
If you guys don't look, it's going to get late...

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:31.760
Sorry.

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:36.730
I'm the only one who's actually looking here...

00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:37.470
Come on.

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:49.920
I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:51.690
Miyauchi-san, calm down!

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:54.660
A ghost! A ghost! A ghost!

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:55.530
Come on...

00:16:57.590 --> 00:17:00.600
Miyauchi-san, calm down, please!

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:11.670
What are you doing?

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:14.200
It was just a little joke.

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:15.970
That's not a joke!

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:17.420
Really?

00:17:17.420 --> 00:17:20.510
I thought it would work well as shock therapy.

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:26.040
Yeah, but now she's seriously shocked.

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:32.300
Everyone! I found it!

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:35.240
Amari-san, way to go!

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:36.070
Here it is!

00:17:37.470 --> 00:17:43.320
"Clad in red clothes, standing in the golden field.

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:45.740
Forge lost connections,

00:17:45.740 --> 00:17:48.790
and lead the people to the cafeteria."

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:50.450
Red clothes?

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:52.320
So, red uniforms?

00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:55.000
Are the third-years' uniforms red?

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:58.800
No, it could be clothes bathed in blood!

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.240
That can't be it.

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:02.080
Red is the color of a leader!

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:04.520
What are you going on about, Miyauchi-san?

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:08.810
I'm more curious about this "golden field" part.

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:12.610
A golden field in the school?

00:18:13.870 --> 00:18:15.490
In that case...

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.110
<b>Gardening Club</b>

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:20.870
A golden field, huh?

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:26.720
Yeah. Is there anything gold-colored in the 
gardens the gardening club manages?

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:29.390
Golden... Golden...

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:32.910
I can't think of anything...

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:38.680
But if you consider yellow a shade of gold, we do.

00:18:38.990 --> 00:18:40.010
What is it?

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:45.880
There are yellow tulips, and yellow pansies.

00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:48.030
Sunflowers are yellow, too.

00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:49.520
Yeah.

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:51.280
I see! Thank you.

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:55.000
But what's the "red clothes" part about, then?

00:18:56.930 --> 00:19:00.460
It could be what Kohinata-san said before,

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:02.490
the third-years' uniforms.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:08.090
"Clad in red clothes, standing in the golden field..."

00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:11.570
So, the third-years stand in 
a field of golden flowers,

00:19:11.570 --> 00:19:13.610
and then after everyone makes up,

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:15.630
they eat together in the cafeteria.

00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:17.840
Maybe that's a little contrived...

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:20.030
That's great, Yuzuko-chan!

00:19:20.030 --> 00:19:23.940
Suddenly Hazuki-san's way into it now, too.

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:27.710
Trying to solve it got to be really fun.

00:19:27.710 --> 00:19:30.520
But if it's only about third-years...

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:33.800
I don't think it'll work for me.

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:36.650
Nagiko-chan-senpai is a second-year.

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:37.890
Oh...

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:40.340
Ah, but don't worry about me.

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:42.660
Let's work to the end to figure out the code.

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:46.280
Okay, everyone, let's go take a look!

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:48.290
Yeah!

00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:01.090
Pansies and tulips are spring flowers.

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:04.470
Flower garden
 currently closed

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:04.470
<b>Wait until spring</b>

00:20:01.610 --> 00:20:04.470
And sunflowers bloom in summer.

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:09.850
You'll have to wait a bit longer 
for the field to become golden.

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:18.570
W-Well, I guess we can't help that.

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:22.630
The code probably only works in the spring.

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:28.620
<b>Sweet 
Potatoes</b>

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:28.620
<b>Only 150</b>

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:36.280
What is it, Momo?

00:20:36.280 --> 00:20:37.240
The potatoes.

00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:37.980
Huh?

00:20:37.980 --> 00:20:39.520
The sweet potatoes!

00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:40.430
What?

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:41.340
What are you talking about?

00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:45.340
Red clothes and a golden field...

00:20:45.670 --> 00:20:48.200
Could this be...

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:48.930
Wait—

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:51.470
Hold on, Momo!

00:20:51.470 --> 00:20:53.230
<b>Sweet Potatoes
 </b>Gardening Club<b></b>

00:20:57.520 --> 00:21:00.190
Oh, everyone...

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:01.440
Look at this.

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:04.150
The potatoes have gotten so big.

00:21:05.830 --> 00:21:06.730
I get it!

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:07.530
Sweet potatoes!

00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:11.160
Red clothes and a golden field.

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:13.440
So this is what it meant!

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:15.590
I've dug up a bunch,

00:21:15.590 --> 00:21:18.670
so please take some home with you.

00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:20.420
Yay!

00:21:25.090 --> 00:21:28.680
It made you that happy?

00:21:33.510 --> 00:21:35.500
Nagiko-chan-senpai,

00:21:36.010 --> 00:21:37.650
what are you doing?

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:39.330
Huh? Oh...

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:45.250
The sweet potatoes seem really 
popular, so I got in the line, but...

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:44.680
<b>Sweet Potatoes</b>

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:44.680
Only 150

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:47.610
There aren't many left, so I'll probably miss out.

00:21:48.140 --> 00:21:49.360
What about you, Momoko?

00:21:49.360 --> 00:21:52.170
Nagiko-chan-senpai, come with me.

00:21:52.170 --> 00:21:53.200
Huh? What?

00:21:58.070 --> 00:21:59.810
She's not here yet?

00:21:59.810 --> 00:22:02.340
There she is! Over here!

00:22:05.640 --> 00:22:08.220
Sweet... potatoes?

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:10.640
Momoko-chan made them.

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:11.600
Momoko did?

00:22:14.450 --> 00:22:17.390
I'd like to thank you all for coming today.

00:22:18.070 --> 00:22:22.980
We've prepared sweet potatoes to 
thank you for all you do for us.

00:22:23.820 --> 00:22:26.400
Time to eat!

00:22:30.800 --> 00:22:31.950
These are good.

00:22:38.390 --> 00:22:39.570
Huh...

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:44.820
Is this really what that code meant?

00:22:44.820 --> 00:22:45.960
What?

00:22:46.390 --> 00:22:48.360
Oh, nothing.

00:22:50.110 --> 00:22:51.000
I'll take another.

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:52.440
Me, too.

00:22:53.400 --> 00:22:54.920
Nagiko-chan-senpai,

00:22:54.920 --> 00:22:58.130
sorry for causing you so 
much trouble all the time.

00:22:58.130 --> 00:23:01.560
Also, thank you for everything.

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:05.910
Shiina-san was absolutely right.

00:23:05.910 --> 00:23:06.360
Huh?

00:23:06.960 --> 00:23:09.650
My classmate told me yesterday.

00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:13.700
And it's terribly rude for people to
assume we're unreliable, too.

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:16.700
You're the one who said that, Haruka.

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:18.910
She doesn't think anything like that.

00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:21.990
You're right. I just thought I'd say it.

00:23:22.970 --> 00:23:25.600
Well, it's a light music club tradition.

00:23:26.080 --> 00:23:28.740
If we build too many walls between the grades,

00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:31.150
it's hard to work together as a band.

00:23:31.150 --> 00:23:34.050
That's why we're used to speaking 
frankly with each other.

00:23:34.440 --> 00:23:37.430
But if you can keep that kind of connection,

00:23:37.430 --> 00:23:41.310
you must care about each other a lot, right?

00:23:42.560 --> 00:23:46.980
You can't do that if you're too polite 
or too friendly just for the sake of it.

00:23:47.440 --> 00:23:50.970
It's because you're truly considerate 
and grateful to each other

00:23:50.970 --> 00:23:54.200
that everyone in your club can be so close.

00:23:54.730 --> 00:23:57.870
Even if everyone is in different grades.

00:24:01.060 --> 00:24:03.750
Thanks for everything, Momoko.

00:24:07.770 --> 00:24:08.630
Yeah!

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:24.840
<b>Preview</b>

00:24:10.690 --> 00:24:12.120
I'm Mahiro Natsume.

00:24:12.120 --> 00:24:14.220
I write novels for fun.

00:24:14.220 --> 00:24:18.220
I think the library is the greatest place ever.

00:24:18.220 --> 00:24:20.730
Next time: Doggy and Scramble.

00:24:18.290 --> 00:24:26.770
<b>Episode 7: Doggy & Scramble</b>

00:24:21.110 --> 00:24:24.540
It'll be about the story I'm working on.
